From 41f717215900eb7d020571b503d1baa53962fc7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Roch=C3=A9=20Compaan?= <roche@upfrontsoftware.co.za>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:56:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] qwen35: reach the dense graph on CUDA

Restructure the single #if defined(__APPLE__) block that wrapped the whole
qwen35 graph so the neutral parts compile on every GPU build:

- qwen35_graph_weights_supported loses its non-Apple refusal and validates the
  layout on both backends.
- qwen4_graph_linear dispatches the gated output norm on the model, not on the
  OS.
- qwen35_graph_attention keeps preparation shared and guards only the verify
  selection, which needs the split-key tables.
- qwen35_graph_stage_inputs and qwen35_graph_forward_tokens are neutral; the
  forward guards its verify probe, the two set_verify_rows calls and the DFlash
  capture begin/capture/end calls, all of which resolve only in ds4_metal.m.
- Block A wraps the verify helpers, Block B the capture helpers, Block C
  verify, commit and the drafter. qwen35_dflash_alloc joins them: its single
  caller is the Metal session setup.
- qwen4_graph_forward_tokens dispatches to the qwen35 graph on both backends.

tests/test_qwen35_host.c includes ../ds4.c and checks the gate with no device
and no model: a dense layout is accepted and prints no verdict, Q6_K output and
per-layer tensors are accepted at block-aligned widths, Q5_K, a Q6_K token
embedding, a width below one block and mismatched alpha/beta are refused. The
link is the second half of the check: any neutral function still calling a
Metal-only symbol fails it.

Not in this commit: the numerical oracle of Step 6, so nothing yet proves the
graph computes the right thing, only that it is reachable and gated.

Verify selection, the split-key row counts and the DFlash capture sit behind five
helpers, so the forward calls them unconditionally and backend differences are
not spread through the graph's control flow. Attention keeps one ordinary
prompt/decode flow and guards only the verify override. The host gate calls the
weight predicate directly; the stderr diversion it used to carry added failure
paths without adding coverage.

